 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Direction Ambiguity:** LIC does not distinguish between positive and negative flow directions; the texture looks the same in both directions [S3].
-*   **Speed Magnitude:** LIC does not display flow speed magnitude [S3].
-*   **Aliasing:** Voxel-based field lines can exhibit a "stair-stepped" aliasing appearance. Trilinear interpolation during rendering can reduce this and create a halo effect for better line separation [S4, unofficial].
+*   **Direction Ambiguity:** LIC does not distinguish between positive and negative flow directions; the texture looks the same in both directions [S4, unofficial].
+*   **Speed Magnitude:** LIC does not display flow speed magnitude [S4, unofficial].
+*   **Aliasing:** Voxel-based field lines can exhibit a "stair-stepped" aliasing appearance. Trilinear interpolation during rendering can reduce this and create a halo effect for better line separation [S5].
 *   **Periodic Motion:** To generate periodic motion effects (e.g., for animation), the phase of the convolution filter function must be shifted during convolution [S2, unofficial].
 
