 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Standard LIC is computationally expensive, as it requires integrating streamlines for every pixel in the field [S1, unofficial][S3]. Optimized versions (e.g., Fast LIC) reduce this by reusing calculations for adjacent pixels along the same streamline [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Requires storage for the vector field, noise texture, and output texture. [Not given in the sources.]
-*   **Strengths:** Densely displays global flow direction information across the entire field without requiring seed points [S3]. Intuitively shows flow field direction with streak-like textures [S3].
-*   **Limitations:** Does not display flow direction (positive/negative) or speed magnitude [S3]. Computationally expensive compared to optimized variants [S1, unofficial].
-*   **When to Use:** When a global overview of flow direction is needed without user interaction for seed points [S3].
-*   **When Not to Use:** When flow direction (sign) or speed magnitude is critical, or when real-time performance is required without optimization techniques [S3].
+*   **Time Complexity:** Standard LIC is computationally expensive, as it requires integrating streamlines for every pixel in the field [S1, unofficial]. Optimized versions (e.g., Fast LIC) reduce this by reusing calculations for adjacent pixels along the same streamline [S1, unofficial].
